{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"b1f928db-fc42-4386-af95-782f1821108d","runId":"19e8cece-ac5f-4cf1-b102-0ee9587d0a71","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":12,"previousEventHash":"sha256:b050c042fdf9f66a032d608024d483f4deba843b4baaba00e87dff7f3f9a59b0","type":"effect.recorded","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a0433e-d47e-700c-afe0-69d5a3e92889","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-27T12:45:43.105Z","idempotencyKey":"effect:github-label:RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi:196:4f859fb6-2cc8-468a-bdac-6d3675591fc5","payload":{"effectType":"github-label","effectId":"github-label:RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi:196:4f859fb6-2cc8-468a-bdac-6d3675591fc5","digest":"sha256:89880e9a2af0fd6cac3c46653d49b723fd9de0723717fad2ff1095794800bc26"}}
{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"920ab14f-bd65-4d95-bddb-d1a761d3935a","runId":"19e8cece-ac5f-4cf1-b102-0ee9587d0a71","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":13,"previousEventHash":"sha256:03d09b0f3158ac6dab5b860fee4453fc35383442b9b7210d476f05e4063d072a","type":"phase.completed","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a0433e-d47e-700c-afe0-69d5a3e92889","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-27T12:46:32.183Z","idempotencyKey":"phase:investigate:1:complete","payload":{"phase":"investigate","attempt":1,"evidence":[],"report":"<!-- FORGE:INVESTIGATOR -->\n## Investigation Report\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Verdict | **Invalid** |\n| Confidence | **High** |\n| Severity | **High** |\n| Task Type | Production-safety regression coverage |\n\n### What Was Claimed\n\nThe pnpm selector list allegedly omitted `--filter-prod`, allowing `pnpm --filter-prod web test` to bypass package-script preflight at the repository root and execute a script from another workspace.\n\n### What We Found\n\nThe frozen `staging` implementation no longer uses an enumerated pnpm selector list. `packageScriptName` rejects any package-manager argument in command position that begins with `-`, so `--filter-prod` fails closed before script lookup. The reported execution bypass is therefore not reproducible on frozen base `7817370b07c7e3d172f4971771e822aab548431a`. Exact regression coverage for pnpm `--filter-prod` is nevertheless absent.\n\n### Root Cause\n\nThe source review finding was overtaken by a broader fail-closed implementation that rejects all package-manager options. The remaining defect is a coverage gap: tests exercise npm selectors but do not pin the reported pnpm spelling, leaving the production-safety invariant implicit.\n\n### Affected Files\n\n| Path | Relevance |\n|---|---|\n| `src/adapters/verification-preflight.ts` | Current fail-closed package-manager option handling; no production change is needed. |\n| `test/adapters/verification-preflight.test.ts` | Add focused pnpm `--filter-prod` regression coverage. |\n\n### Evidence\n\n- `packageScriptName` throws `unsupportedPackageManagerOptionsError` whenever the package-manager command position starts with `-`.\n- Existing selector regression coverage includes npm `--prefix` and `--workspace`, but not pnpm `--filter-prod`.\n- Preflight validates executable availability before package-manager parsing, so the fixture must expose a pnpm executable to exercise the intended branch.\n\n### History Findings\n\n- Issue `#196` was generated from correctness finding `correctness-argv-3` on PR `#192` at head `d731df0c59a6c3bd3b36fcde512c759ab6625ae0`.\n- Frozen integration base `7817370b07c7e3d172f4971771e822aab548431a` contains broader fail-closed option rejection, superseding the selector-list implementation described by the finding.\n\n### Recommendation\n\nAdd a focused regression case proving `pnpm --filter-prod web test` is rejected as unsupported package-manager option input. Do not alter production parsing because the current generic rejection is stricter and already closes the reported bypass.\n\n### Related Issues\n\n- Source issue `#111`\n- Source PR `#192`\n\n### Decomposition Assessment\n\nNo decomposition is required. The work is a single focused test change in one adapter test file.\n\n### Acceptance Spec\n\n- [x] Validate the reported argv against the frozen integration implementation.\n- [ ] Add focused coverage for pnpm `--filter-prod`.\n- [ ] Pass the required `check` verification command.\n- [ ] Complete fresh correctness and security review at the exact remediation head.\n\n<!-- INVESTIGATION:COMPLETE -->","outputArtifactHash":"sha256:investigate-196-filter-prod"}}
